  ],
  "residual_risks": [
    "Even with fixed ticks, force layouts can show small cross-browser floating-point differences; tasks that require pixel-perfect layouts may still need additional rounding or a post-relaxation snap step.",
    "Opening HTML via file:// may block fetch() / d3.csv() in some browsers; tasks may still require running a local static server despite using relative paths.",
    "If an implementation attaches events to <circle> but forgets to disable pointer events on <text>, click/hover may remain flaky; the new guidance reduces but cannot prevent misuse."
  ]
}
